# Line endings.
#
# Every text file in this repository is stored with LF endings, and that is
# already true of every file committed so far. Without this file, whether you
# get LF or CRLF in your working copy depends on your own core.autocrlf, which
# is why the same checkout here currently holds LF HTML next to CRLF CSS, and
# why git kept warning that it would swap one for the other.
#
# eol=lf settles it: LF in the repository and LF on disk, on every machine.
# That matches what Cloudflare serves, and it means a diff only ever shows
# lines somebody actually changed. Nothing needs CRLF here; there are no
# batch or shell scripts in this repo.
#
# Adding this changes no committed content. It was verified with
# "git add --renormalize ." reporting nothing to stage.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Git usually detects these on its own, but saying so is safer than
# trusting detection: a font or a photograph run through line ending
# conversion is a corrupt file, not a messy diff.

*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary

*.pdf   binary
